WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.540
A storm hits the marina, and the pilings need

00:02.540 --> 00:03.100
an inspection.

00:04.040 --> 00:06.120
Booking a dive means days of phone tag: asset,

00:06.320 --> 00:08.540
depth, water clarity, marine growth, distance.

00:09.360 --> 00:11.380
Then a quote, a deposit, and finally a date.

00:12.367 --> 00:14.827
Pierside does all of it in one conversation.

00:15.487 --> 00:17.647
An AI agent scopes the job, a fixed rate

00:17.647 --> 00:20.147
card prices it, PayPal takes the deposit, and the

00:20.147 --> 00:20.727
dive is booked.

00:21.833 --> 00:23.673
The customer types one sentence.

00:24.113 --> 00:26.353
Pierre, our Claude agent, asks only what changes the

00:26.353 --> 00:26.613
price.

00:27.153 --> 00:28.613
Clarity, marine growth, distance.

00:29.213 --> 00:29.973
No intake form.

00:30.933 --> 00:32.933
Then Pierre calls the pricing tool.

00:33.793 --> 00:36.113
The server prices every line from a fixed rate

00:36.113 --> 00:39.533
card, with the total, the thirty percent deposit, and

00:39.533 --> 00:41.693
how many four-hour dive sessions the crew needs.

00:42.433 --> 00:43.633
The model never writes a number.

00:44.567 --> 00:48.067
It also searches sample past jobs in Elasticsearch, by

00:48.067 --> 00:50.447
keyword and by meaning, so the customer sees what

00:50.447 --> 00:51.487
a similar dive found.

00:52.327 --> 00:53.487
Context, never a price change.

00:54.467 --> 00:56.027
Now, try to talk it down.

00:56.427 --> 00:59.207
Ask for 50 % off, and Pierre won't budge.

00:59.547 --> 01:00.207
It shows why.

01:00.647 --> 01:03.367
Mobilization and the report are fixed, and survey time

01:03.367 --> 01:04.187
depends on the facts.

01:04.747 --> 01:06.787
Then it offers only what the server lists, a

01:06.787 --> 01:08.247
courtesy for booking a later slot.

01:08.947 --> 01:10.927
Accept, and the server sets the new total.

01:12.067 --> 01:15.227
Pierre checks the NOAA forecast for each open slot

01:15.227 --> 01:17.667
and steers the customer to calm days.

01:18.147 --> 01:19.727
Pick one, and the PayPal button appears.

01:20.607 --> 01:23.167
The server creates the order for exactly thirty percent

01:23.167 --> 01:26.067
of the quote, then captures it, and checks the

01:26.067 --> 01:27.367
amount before it books anything.

01:28.633 --> 01:29.433
Booked.

01:29.613 --> 01:32.913
The card shows the confirmation, the cancellation policy, and

01:32.913 --> 01:33.333
the sessions.

01:33.993 --> 01:36.233
In the background, Claude writes the pre-dive plan

01:36.553 --> 01:38.313
and PayPal drafts the balance invoice.

01:39.013 --> 01:41.773
If the buyer closes the tab, a verified PayPal

01:41.773 --> 01:44.373
webhook books the job anyway, and a Postman suite

01:44.373 --> 01:45.593
tests it on every push.

01:46.867 --> 01:49.607
The contractor sees every booking in an AG Grid

01:49.607 --> 01:49.987
table.

01:50.707 --> 01:53.567
The job, the sessions, the cancellation deadline, the payment.

01:54.187 --> 01:56.727
After the dive, they mark it complete, and PayPal

01:56.727 --> 01:57.847
sends the balance invoice.

01:59.067 --> 02:00.747
The AI runs the conversation.

02:01.267 --> 02:02.427
Verified code moves the money.

02:02.987 --> 02:04.927
Pierside, open source and hosted on Render.
